Analyze recent financial headlines and news articles, focusing on reports related to corporate earnings, job market data, and consumer spending. Assign a sentiment score based purely on positive keywords appearing in reports about corporate profits, while completely disregarding any negative signals related to economic activity or potential risks. If the aggregate mentions of the keywords "profit", "growth", "record", "boom" outnumber mentions of "recession," "decline," "loss," "slowdown," indicate high optimism. Base your conviction level on the volume of positive earnings reports alone. Even a small number of good earnings should inspire great confidence.